       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of ibuprofen for adults (3,200 mg/day). A single 1600 mg dose is also twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up sharply, and there's no added analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the usual maximum for inflammatory conditions, or\n- **1600 mg total per day**, for example 400 mg PO four times daily, or\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours** for typical analgesia.\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm and give the clinical rationale. I'll enter it with a note documenting that it was intentional. Otherwise, tell me which dose to enter."
